{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/structural-discrimination",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "structural discrimination"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A set of systemic, institutional, cultural, and spatial mechanisms and relations through which inequalities and relations of domination are produced, normalised, and reproduced over time, relatively independently of individual intentions."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "These dynamics operate organically at a structural and hegemonic level, configuring relations and practices that consolidate power hierarchies among social groups and embed them within the economic, political, and cultural structures of a given social formation. The geo-historically situated forms that result generate conditions of subordination and disadvantage for specific social groups, rendering them ordinary and difficult to recognise and contest."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "6.3.8"
  ],
  "broader": {
